# ─── Build output & dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
.next-build/
out/
build/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every env form, not just the .local variants. This repository is public and
# needs none of these to build: the enquiry form is a public Monday embed and
# every contact detail on the site is already published. If an email provider is
# added later its key belongs in Vercel's environment variables, never here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# ─── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-off diagnostics and commit-message drafts. Anything worth keeping was
# folded into scripts/ as a real, documented audit.
_*.mjs
_*.js
msg*.txt
*.bak
*.log
design-review/_prod.*
public/_grade-preview.html

# ─── Withheld frames — MUST NOT be published ──────────────────────────────────
# Pulled in Phase 6 §4 and deliberately absent from the public tree. They remain
# in local history. Rationale for each is in design-review/imagery-report.md and
# design-review/publish-manifest.md; `npm run publish:manifest` fails if any of
# them is ever referenced again.
public/media/olLK_LD_072.jpg
public/media/spire2.png
public/media/thspire2.png
public/media/stHARLEY.jpg
public/media/blDSC_9849.jpg
public/media/ae9Z8A4481-Edit.jpg
public/media/aeIMG_2133.jpg

# ─── Raw camera masters ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 125 MB of source footage. `content/*.ts` records each one in an `original:`
# field so every transcode's provenance is documented, but nothing serves them —
# the site plays the web transcodes in public/media/video/, which ARE committed.
public/media/Wedding clip.mp4
public/media/xorafi.mp4
public/media/paDJI_2288.MP4
public/media/paDJI_2282.mp4
public/media/jdIMG_8749.MOV
public/media/deIMG_8840.MOV
public/media/deIMG_8845.MOV

# ─── Unreferenced leftovers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# posterimage.png is a 3 MB frame of a real couple's ceremony, superseded in §6
# by an optimised poster. Nothing links to it and it shows identifiable people,
# so it does not go to a public repository.
public/media/posterimage.png
public/media/about_updated.png
public/assets/img/close-icon.svg

# Villa Aetos was withdrawn from the collection by the owner, so its ten
# photographs are orphaned — no reference in content/ or src/. They follow the
# manifest's orphan rule rather than lingering as dead weight in a public
# repository. Still on local disk; the venue can be restored from history.
public/media/ae9Z8A4450-Edit.jpg
public/media/ae9Z8A4452-Edit.jpg
public/media/ae9Z8A4458.jpg
public/media/ae9Z8A4482.jpg
public/media/ae12.2023 _ 2.jpg
public/media/aeIMG_2088.jpg
public/media/aeIMG_2102.jpg
public/media/aeIMG_2122.jpg
public/media/aeIMG_2131.jpg
public/media/aeIMG_6743_4_5.jpg

# ─── Review screenshots ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# design-review/ IS published — it is how a reviewer sees the build without
# running it.
#
# The eight superseded round-by-round sets were DELETED outright in the final QA
# pass rather than merely ignored, so the repository cannot show two eras of the
# design at once. Everything current is published: final/, final-scroll/,
# contact-sheets/, directions/, grade/, atmosphere/, graffiti/, stats/ and every
# report. All of it is reproducible — see design-review/publish-manifest.md.
#
# cross-browser/ stays out: it is raw engine probe output, superseded by the
# summary in the report.
design-review/cross-browser/
.dns-watch/
